<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Manapii</h1><p class="st-meta">100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">People of south-east Ireland named by Ptolemy, with a town called Manapia, sharing their name with the Menapii of the Low Countries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geography-ptolemy">Ptolemy's Geography</a> of about 150 places the Manapii on the east coast of Ireland, south of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cauci">Cauci</a>, usually located around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-wicklow">Wicklow</a> or north <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-wexford">Wexford</a>, with a settlement named Manapia. Their name matches the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/menapii">Menapii</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-belgica">Belgic Gaul</a>, which has led to suggestions of migration or trading links across the sea.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of their rulers or society. Some scholars connect them with later Irish population names such as the Monaig, recorded in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-leinster">Leinster</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/northern-ireland">Ulster</a>, and with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-fermanagh">Fir Manach</a> who gave their name to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-fermanagh">Fermanagh</a>, but these links rest only on the similarity of names.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Manapii do not appear in later records. Their part of the coast later lay within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-leinster">Kingdom of Leinster</a>, and especially the lands of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ui-chennselaig">Ui Chennselaig</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/manapii.jpg" alt="Manapii" width="320" height="409"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ptolemy%27s_Ireland.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Goidelic Celtic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=manapii" aria-label="Manapii on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4483 351 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Manapii lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4803 607h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4803 607h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Ireland. <a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=manapii">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

